From 741d2b2808f1ad3bd448245ee86cf75e6282b0fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:29:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 65/65] Species scale: NUM_DIGIMON 1024, per-partner rows in
 the DIGI.DAT records, wide flags, tournament/VS tables

- NUM_DIGIMON 1024; the resident per-partner tables (RAISE_DATA, EVOLUTION_REQS/GAINS,
  ITEM_TAKE_DISTANCE, VLALL ids, TRN/TRN2 rows) keep the 180 originals' rows; a new species'
  rows come from its record through the (now 16-slot) cache: RAISE_ROW, EVO_REQ_ROW, EVO_GAINS_ROW,
  getItemTakeDistance, getPartnerVlallSoundId, getEvolutionPath
- DIGI.DAT v2: index sectors (partner list, first Mega, evolution links with the originals)
- raised/recruited flags of species without a trigger: two saved bitsets in the v2 extension
- lab menu: every partner species of DIGI.DAT (L1/R1 jump 10)
- tournament/VS name, portrait and sprite tables never read past their end; PARTICIPANT_TYPES u16
- getSpeciesPara no longer recurses for an undefined id

